# Python bytecode caches (created by running scripts/*.py and tests)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Probe leftovers. scripts/probe_plugin.py removes its workspace only when the run PASSES —
# a failing probe deliberately keeps both of these for debugging, which is exactly when a
# maintainer is least likely to notice them in `git status`.
.probe-tmp/
probe-transcript.jsonl

# Acceptance-evidence run logs (probe sessions). Raw session streams can
# carry repository content and belong beside the round's other transient evidence, never in
# the tree.
.probe-run.log

.claude/worktrees/

# Codex writes this install marker into a marketplace snapshot when `codex plugin add` runs. On a
# host whose only copy of the fleet IS that snapshot, the marker sits in the tree permanently and
# would show as an untracked change on every `git status`. Anchored with a leading slash: Codex writes the marker only at the snapshot root,
# and a slashless pattern matches the basename at EVERY depth — measured, a nested
# `tests/fixtures/.codex-marketplace-install.json` is reported with the anchor and silently hidden
# without it. A nested occurrence is somebody's real local addition and must still reach the
# operator (review finding, PR #130).
/.codex-marketplace-install.json

# Tooling caches from the dev dependency group (pyproject.toml); nothing in them is evidence.
.venv/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# Routing cases generated per run by scripts/eval_routing.py, with the `claude plugin eval`
# results and report written beneath them.
evals/generated/
